[{:seon.task/name "a-measures-calls-are-its-own-threads"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by web-2, 2026-11-15 [M]: seon.profile's call counters are process-wide (its docstring says so), so a cost proof's :calls counts any thread still running beside the measure: seon.render-cost-test's first-page proof went green and red at one digest (2,455 / 2,463 calls), its walk's own count the same in 30 runs alone or after the render suite. A verdict that reads what other threads did is no verdict (docs/principles.md#6-nothing-changed-nothing-runs-a-change-costs-what-it-touched). Ticks and bytes are measured on the measuring thread already; calls are not. Correct: the counters of seon.profile/measure! count the calls of the measuring fiber or thread only, as its ticks and bytes do, so every :calls bound judges its own work; :calls stays a dimension (it is the one that names an extra pass). web-2 restated its one proof in ticks and bytes meanwhile (26f6f12b5f). Estimate: one thread-identity compare a counted call. Proof, red first: a measure while another thread calls a contracted function in a loop counts only the measured thunk's calls."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.profile-test/a-measures-calls-are-its-own-threads}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-native-definition-loads-in-place-or-restarts"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-11-15 by context [M]: f9969ae8ca added seon-profile-over! inside seon.profile's scheme-defs, a defonce; bin/update loaded the landing in place (the binary digest counts no src change), procs re-resolved :over! to nil in root and the fork server, and every agent's seon.agent/init! threw at start (round 2 paused). Fixed forward by moving the definition into a plain def and resolving it at its call. The class: a src form that defines native (scm/eval-string) state inside a defonce is skipped by an in-place load, so the running process and its forks run code whose native half is missing. Design to write: either such forms are never defonce (each scm block idempotent, re-evaluated by a load), or seon.system/restart-for counts a changed native block as a reason to restart. Check: a law over src flags scm/eval-string inside defonce. Proof, red first: a landing that adds a native definition is loaded in place and the procedure it names resolves. Owner: runtime."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.profile-test/a-native-definition-added-by-a-landing-resolves-after-it-loads}}]
